; The canonical change from S7 to S8.
;
; S7 |- S8. The language definitions are Strata's now.
;
; Every language in the tree -- twenty grammars, from a five-line one for
; plain text to a hundred and thirty for Lean -- is read with an artifact
; elaborated from a grammar source. That elaboration was Meta's. It is now
; also Strata's, and the two agree: for every grammar, the artifact Strata
; produces is the artifact that was already committed, byte for byte.
;
; Two things had to change for that to be writable at all. A text literal in
; Strata denoted its own spelling, quotes and backslashes included, which no
; elaborator survives; it now denotes what it spells. And the literal syntax
; had no escapes, so a grammar's own patterns could not be written down; it
; now has them.
;
; Neither is an addition to what Strata can compute. Both are the language
; ceasing to be wrong about text.
(change
  (kind foundation)
  (name "S7->S8")
  (predecessor (foundation-of "foundations/S7"))
  (delta-meta (file "changes/S7-S8/delta-meta.canon"))
  (delta-grammar (file "changes/S7-S8/delta-grammar.canon"))
  (feature
    (feature
      (name "language definitions rewritten")
      (programs [
        (file "features/strata/language.generated.meta")
      ])
      (sources [
        (text-file "features/strata/language.meta")
        (text-file "languages/strata/strata.grammar")
        (text-file "languages/strata/strata.meta")
        (text-file "strata/system/grammar.strata")
      ]))))
